Architecture: all
Maintainer: TuxDrive contributors <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, python3-cryptography (>= 46.0.5), python3-nautilus, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, libsecret-tools, fuse3, openssh-client, tor, torsocks, obfs4proxy, miniupnpc, natpmpc, network-manager, qrencode, zbar-tools, xdg-utils, ca-certificates
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Breaks: tuxdrive (<< 0.15.1)
Replaces: tuxdrive (<< 0.15.1)
Homepage: https://github.com/tpluharik/Tuxdrive
Description: Private peer and multi-provider cloud storage client for Ubuntu
 TuxDrive provides browser-based OAuth, automatic transfer-engine bootstrap,
 eight cloud providers, encrypted provider-linked profile backup and device migration, adaptive capability controls, sync-health and audit dashboards, optional Nautilus actions/status, block-delta planning, NAT/relay peer connectivity, per-file offline controls, policy-aware transfers, role-based multi-peer sharing, expiring encrypted file drops, LAN/QR pairing, edit leases, multiple accounts, two-way and
 one-way synchronization, selective folders, conflict handling, tray controls,
 Tor v3 Onion Services with per-device authorization and fail-closed privacy
 policies, notifications, in-app verified updates, and files-on-demand virtual drives
 through rclone and FUSE.
